// Title: Windows Security event log cleared
// Data source table: SecurityEvent
// What it detects: Windows event 1102 (the audit log was cleared). Intruders clear the Security log to
//   remove evidence of their activity, so any occurrence deserves review.
// Likely false positives: Administrators clearing logs during troubleshooting or rebuilds; imaging and
//   decommissioning of lab machines; a log management script run on a schedule.
// MITRE ATT&CK technique: T1070.001 Indicator Removal: Clear Windows Event Logs
// Tuning notes: Keep this at a very low threshold: there are few legitimate reasons and the event is
//   cheap. Event 1102 names who cleared the log in SubjectUserName and SubjectDomainName. Clearing the
//   System log is a separate event (104, source Microsoft-Windows-Eventlog) in the Event table; add a
//   second query for it if you collect that log. Because the log is cleared, rely on the copy already
//   forwarded to Sentinel rather than the host.
// Status: Written against the documented SecurityEvent schema. Not yet run in a live Sentinel workspace.

let lookback = 1d;
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where EventID == 1102
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    Computer,
    ClearedBy = strcat(SubjectDomainName, "\\", SubjectUserName),
    SubjectLogonId,
    Activity
| order by TimeGenerated desc
